  "cards": [
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Primary path: POST /api/rectify", "items": [
      "Silence or noise returns empty text and no audio; the recording is never echoed back",
      "WS /ws/rectify runs the same steps per utterance, on the same rate budget",
      "A broken saved voice returns the text with no audio; no other voice speaks for the patient",
      "Database reads run while the recogniser does",
      "Measured 2026-10-25 (RTX 3050 on mains power, live Supabase, warm): the patient waits median 772 ms, p90 1,190 ms; ~480 ms is the sign-in check and rate limit (two ~220 ms database round trips), ASR ~140 ms"
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Trust boundaries", "items": [
      "Clients hold only the public anon key and their own JWT; the service-role key stays on the server",
      "Clients can call Supabase directly, so row-level security, not the API, is the real wall",
      "Live attack (scripts/attack_live.py): 40 of 40 attempts blocked on 2026-10-25"
    ] },
    { "dot": "violet", "title": "Learning loop", "items": [
      "POST /api/sessions/{id}/utterances: the patient's yes/no teaches word fixes (FeedbackEngine) and their vocabulary",
      "Only the server writes what it learns (migration 20261031)",
      "Snapping is on only while the patient repeats known words"
    ] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "Clinicians and reports", "items": [
      "A verified clinician reads a patient only after redeeming that patient's link code",
      "The PDF is built from stored rows under the caller's JWT; nothing clinical comes from the request"
    ] },
    { "dot": "slate", "title": "Not drawn", "items": [
      "The frontend (epako_sylva_experience.html) is a mock, not yet wired to the API",
      "Voice banking, voice sculpt and /api/biomarkers routes",
      "Rate limiter state lives in Postgres (rate_limit_hit RPC, service key)"
    ] }
  ]
